<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,844,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,844,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors</p>
<p>Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members</p>
<p>(crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 08/28/96    08/21/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 22,844,000  24,004,000   23,974,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  66,720	74,404	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   08/28/96    08/21/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,059,000   4,324,000    4,547,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,092,000   3,173,000    3,750,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,545,000   4,252,000    4,104,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,922,000   2,745,000    2,031,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,630,000   3,596,000    3,412,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 3,783,000   3,994,000    4,227,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,813,000   1,921,000    1,903,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	22,844,000  24,004,000   23,974,000</p>
</text>
